 a common benchmark for crowd counting.\n","\n","Part B generally represents relatively less congested scenes compared with Part A."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"7ed5cf94","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:09:50.611809Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:09:50.611443Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.69406Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.693258Z"},"papermill":{"duration":13.093396,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.695797+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:09:50.602401+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Total samples: 400\n","Training samples: 360\n","Validation samples: 40\n"]}],"source":["from torch.utils.data import Subset\n","\n","train_root_dir = \"/kaggle/input/datasets/tthien/shanghaitech/ShanghaiTech/part_B/train_data\"\n","\n","train_root_data = EnhancedShanghaiTechDataset(\n","    train_root_dir,\n","    gt_downsample=4,\n","    shuffle=False\n",")\n","\n","# Split 90% of the training set for training\n","# and 10% for validation\n","train_size = int(0.9 * len(train_root_data))\n","val_size = len(train_root_data) - train_size\n","\n","# Indices for train and validation\n","indices = list(range(len(train_root_data)))\n","\n","train_indices = indices[:train_size]\n","val_indices = indices[train_size:]\n","\n","# Create training and validation subsets\n","train_dataset = Subset(train_root_data, train_indices)\n","val_dataset = Subset(train_root_data, val_indices)\n","\n","print(\"Total samples:\", len(train_root_data))\n","print(\"Training samples:\", len(train_dataset))\n","print(\"Validation samples:\", len(val_dataset))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1fe1640f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.008339,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.712871+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.704532+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Train/validation/test split\n","\n","```text\n","90% → training\n","10% → validation\n","```\n","\n","The original test set remains separate.\n","\n","### Why validation?\n","\n","You don't want to judge the model using only training data.\n","\n","Training data tells you:\n","\n","> How well can the model memorize/fit the training examples?\n","\n","Validation data tells you:\n","\n","> How well is the model performing on unseen samples during development?\n","\n","Test data should be reserved for final evaluation.\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","Training\n","   ↓\n","Model learning\n","\n","Validation\n","   ↓\n","Model selection / monitoring\n","\n","Test\n","   ↓\n","Final evaluation\n","```\n","\n","### Subset\n","\n","Subset allows you to create a smaller dataset from an existing dataset by specifying which indices/samples you want to use.\n","\n","### Complete Flow\n","\n","```\n","                 train_root_data\n","                   400 samples\n","                        │\n","                        ↓\n","                Shuffle the indices\n","                        │\n","             ┌──────────┴──────────┐\n","             ↓                     ↓\n","       90% Training            10% Validation\n","        360 samples              40 samples\n","             │                     │\n","             ↓                     ↓\n","      train_dataset          val_dataset\n","```"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"a2794366","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.7313Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.73103Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.953636Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.952758Z"},"papermill":{"duration":10.233996,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.955308+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:03.721312+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Number of batches in train_loader: 45\n","Number of batches in val_loader: 5\n","Number of batches in test_loader: 40\n"]}],"source":["from torch.utils.data import DataLoader\n","\n","batch_size = 8\n","\n","train_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False, pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available())\n","val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False, pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available())\n","\n","# ✅ Test set\n","test_root_dir = \"/kaggle/input/datasets/tthien/shanghaitech/ShanghaiTech/part_B/test_data\"\n","test_set = EnhancedShanghaiTechDataset(test_root_dir, gt_downsample=4, shuffle=False)\n","test_loader = DataLoader(test_set, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False, pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available())\n","\n","print(\"Number of batches in train_loader:\", len(train_loader))\n","print(\"Number of batches in val_loader:\", len(val_loader))\n","print(\"Number of batches in test_loader:\", len(test_loader))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a89f74c2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.0087,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.972934+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.964234+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## DataLoader\n","\n","DataLoader, which takes a dataset and provides batches of samples.\n","\n","Instead of giving the model one image at a time, you can give it multiple images together.\n","\n","The code uses `batch_size = 8`. Therefore, the model processes:\n","\n","```text\n","8 images\n","```\n","\n","at a time.\n","\n","The DataLoader handles:\n","\n","* batching\n","* shuffling\n","* iteration\n","* memory transfer\n","\n","```\n","                 ShanghaiTech Part B\n","                         │\n","             ┌───────────┴───────────┐\n","             │                       │\n","        Training data             Test data\n","             │                       │\n","          90% / 10%                100%\n","             │                       │\n","       ┌─────┴─────┐                 │\n","       │           │                 │\n","     Train        Val              Test\n","       │           │                 │\n","       ▼           ▼                 ▼\n"," train_loader  val_loader       test_loader\n","       │           │                 │\n","       └───────────┴─────────────────┘\n","                       │\n","                  batch size = 8\n","```"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"b9cacc5a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.992279Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.991853Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.003003Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.00239Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.022533,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.004397+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:13.981864+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["import torch.nn as nn\n","import torch.nn.functional as F\n","\n","class FourColumnMCNN(nn.Module):\n","    def __init__(self):\n","        super(FourColumnMCNN, self).__init__()\n","\n","        # ✅ Very Large Receptive Field Column\n","        self.column1 = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Conv2d(3, 16, kernel_size=11, padding=5),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(16),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(16, 32, kernel_size=9, padding=4),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(32),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(32, 64, kernel_size=7, padding=3),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(64),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","        )\n","\n","        # ✅ Large Receptive Field Column\n","        self.column2 = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Conv2d(3, 16, kernel_size=9, padding=4),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(16),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(16, 32, kernel_size=7, padding=3),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(32),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(32, 64, kernel_size=5, padding=2),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(64),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","        )\n","\n","        # ✅ Medium Receptive Field Column\n","        self.column3 = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Conv2d(3, 20, kernel_size=7, padding=3),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(20),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(20, 40, kernel_size=5, padding=2),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(40),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(40, 80, kernel_size=3, padding=1),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(80),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","        )\n","\n","        # ✅ Small Receptive Field Column (fine details for dense crowds)\n","        self.column4 = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Conv2d(3, 24, kernel_size=5, padding=2),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(24),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(24, 48, kernel_size=3, padding=1),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(48),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.MaxPool2d(2),\n","\n","            nn.Conv2d(48, 96, kernel_size=3, padding=1),\n","            nn.BatchNorm2d(96),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","        )\n","\n","        # ✅ Fusion Layer\n","        self.fusion = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Conv2d(64 + 64 + 80 + 96, 64, kernel_size=1),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.Conv2d(64, 1, kernel_size=1),\n","            nn.ReLU()\n","        )\n","\n","    def forward(self, x):\n","        x1 = self.column1(x)\n","        x2 = self.column2(x)\n","        x3 = self.column3(x)\n","        x4 = self.column4(x)\n","\n","        x_cat = torch.cat((x1, x2, x3, x4), dim=1)\n","        out = self.fusion(x_cat)\n","        return out"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7521953e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00838,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.021423+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.013043+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Four Column MCNN\n","\n","This is the heart of the system.\n","\n","The basic idea is:\n","\n","```text\n","                   Input image\n","                       │\n","       ┌───────────────┼───────┐\n","       │       │       │       │\n","       ▼       ▼       ▼       ▼\n","   Column 1 Column 2 Column 3 Column 4\n","       │       │       │       │\n","       └───────┴───────┴───────┘\n","                       │\n","                    Concatenate\n","                       │\n","                    Fusion\n","                       │\n","                       ▼\n","                Density Map\n","```\n","\n","![MCNN Architecture](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/spl_03/main/images/dense/mcnn/architecture.png)\n","\n","## Multiple Columns\n","\n","People can appear at different scales.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","Large person\n","      ↓\n","████████\n","\n","Medium person\n","      ↓\n"," █████\n","\n","Tiny distant person\n","      ↓\n"," ██\n","```\n","\n","A single convolutional scale may not handle all of them equally well.\n","\n","MCNN therefore uses different convolution kernel sizes.\n","\n","Your four columns represent:\n","\n","1. Very large receptive field\n","2. Large receptive field\n","3. Medium receptive field\n","4. Small receptive field\n","\n","The implementation is explicitly structured this way. \n","\n","## Receptive Field\n","\n","This is essential for understanding MCNN.\n","\n","A convolution kernel looks at a local area.\n","\n","For:\n","\n","```text\n","3×3\n","```\n","\n","the neuron sees a small neighborhood.\n","\n","For:\n","\n","```text\n","11×11\n","```\n","\n","it sees a much larger neighborhood.\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","3×3 → local detail\n","7×7 → larger context\n","11×11 → even larger context\n","```\n","\n","This helps the network deal with different crowd scales.\n","\n","### Why small receptive fields help dense crowds?\n","\n","In very dense scenes, people can be tiny.\n","\n","You don't necessarily need a huge region.\n","\n","Instead, fine local patterns such as:\n","\n","```text\n","head\n","shoulder\n","small person structure\n","```\n","\n","can be important.\n","\n","So Column 4 focuses more on local details.\n","\n","\n","## Batch Normalization\n","\n","Batch Normalization normalizes intermediate feature activations.\n","\n","Conceptually:\n","\n","```text\n","Conv\n"," ↓\n","BatchNorm\n"," ↓\n","ReLU\n","```\n","\n","It can make training more stable.\n","\n","\n","## ReLU\n","\n","ReLU is:\n","\n","$$\n","f(x)=\\max(0,x)\n","$$\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","-5 → 0\n","-1 → 0\n"," 0 → 0\n"," 2 → 2\n"," 7 → 7\n","```\n","\n","It introduces non-linearity.\n","\n","## Max Pooling\n","\n","This reduces spatial dimensions by approximately half.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","768 × 768\n","```\n","\n","becomes:\n","\n","```text\n","384 × 384\n","```\n","\n","and another pooling:\n","\n","```text\n","384 × 384\n","```\n","\n","becomes:\n","\n","```text\n","192 × 192\n","```\n","\n","This is consistent with your density-map output resolution.\n","\n","## Feature-map sizes\n","\n","Starting with:\n","\n","```text\n","768 × 768\n","```\n","\n","Each column has two pooling layers.\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","```text\n","768\n"," ↓ pool\n","384\n"," ↓ pool\n","192\n","```\n","\n","So every column eventually produces:\n","\n","```text\n","192 × 192\n","```\n","\n","This is very important because the four branches need matching spatial dimensions before concatenation.\n","\n","## Channel dimensions\n","\n","At the end:\n","\n","1. **Column 1:** 64 channels\n","2. **Column 2:** 64 channels\n","3. **Column 3:** 80 channels\n","4. **Column 4:** 96 channels\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","$$\n","64+64+80+96=304\n","$$\n","\n","So the combined tensor contains:\n","\n","```text\n","304 channels\n","```\n","\n","## Concatenation\n","\n","The forward function:\n","\n","```python\n","x1 = self.column1(x)\n","x2 = self.column2(x)\n","x3 = self.column3(x)\n","x4 = self.column4(x)\n","\n","x_cat = torch.cat((x1,x2,x3,x4),dim=1)\n","```\n","\n","Concatenates along the channel dimension.\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","Column 1 → [B,64,192,192]\n","Column 2 → [B,64,192,192]\n","Column 3 → [B,80,192,192]\n","Column 4 → [B,96,192,192]\n","```\n","\n","becomes:\n","\n","```text\n","[B,304,192,192]\n","```\n","\n","## Fusion layer\n","\n","The fusion layer is:\n","\n","```python\n","nn.Conv2d(304,64,kernel_size=1)\n","```\n","\n","Why a 1×1 convolution?\n","\n","Because it combines information across channels.\n","\n","You can think of it as:\n","\n","```text\n","304 feature channels\n","        ↓\n","learn how to combine them\n","        ↓\n","64 feature channels\n","```\n","\n","without changing:\n","\n","```text\n","192 × 192\n","```\n","\n","spatial dimensions.\n","\n","## Second fusion convolution\n","\n","Then:\n","\n","```python\n","nn.Conv2d(64,1,kernel_size=1)\n","```\n","\n","reduces:\n","\n","```text\n","64 channels\n","```\n","\n","to:\n","\n","```text\n","1 channel\n","```\n","\n","That one channel is:\n","\n","> the predicted density map.\n","\n","## Why ReLU at the output?\n","\n","The final layer is:\n","\n","```python\n","nn.ReLU()\n","```\n","\n","Density values should normally be non-negative.\n","\n","You don't want:\n","\n","```text\n","-0.8 people density\n","```\n","\n","So ReLU ensures:\n","\n","$$\n","D(x,y)\\ge0\n","$$\n","\n","\n","## Complete model architecture\n","\n","Your model can therefore be represented as:\n","\n","```text\n","                       INPUT\n","                    3×768×768\n","                         │\n","          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐\n","          │              │              │\n","          ▼              ▼              ▼\n","      Column 1       Column 2       Column 3       Column 4\n","      11×11          9×9            7×7            5×5\n","        ↓              ↓              ↓              ↓\n","      9×9            7×7            5×5            3×3\n","        ↓              ↓              ↓              ↓\n","      7×7            5×5            3×3            3×3\n","        │              │              │              │\n","       64             64             80             96\n","        └──────────────┴──────────────┴──────────────┘\n","                              │\n","                       Concatenate\n","                              │\n","                         304 channels\n","                              │\n","                           1×1 Conv\n","                              │\n","                          64 channels\n","                              │\n","                           ReLU\n","                              │\n","                           1×1 Conv\n","                              │\n","                           1 channel\n","                              │\n","                           ReLU\n","                              │\n","                    Predicted Density Map\n","                         192×192\n","```"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"id":"cbaef7be","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.039782Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.039246Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.333966Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.333324Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.306166,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.335885+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.029719+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["model = (FourColumnMCNN().to(DEVICE))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"66f5ce68","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.355105Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.354695Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.360875Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.360049Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.017579,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.362606+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.345027+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["FourColumnMCNN(\n","  (column1): Sequential(\n","    (0): Conv2d(3, 16, kernel_size=(11, 11), stride=(1, 1), padding=(5, 5))\n","    (1): BatchNorm2d(16, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (2): ReLU()\n","    (3): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (4): Conv2d(16, 32, kernel_size=(9, 9), stride=(1, 1), padding=(4, 4))\n","    (5): BatchNorm2d(32, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (6): ReLU()\n","    (7): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (8): Conv2d(32, 64, kernel_size=(7, 7), stride=(1, 1), padding=(3, 3))\n","    (9): BatchNorm2d(64, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (10): ReLU()\n","  )\n","  (column2): Sequential(\n","    (0): Conv2d(3, 16, kernel_size=(9, 9), stride=(1, 1), padding=(4, 4))\n","    (1): BatchNorm2d(16, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (2): ReLU()\n","    (3): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (4): Conv2d(16, 32, kernel_size=(7, 7), stride=(1, 1), padding=(3, 3))\n","    (5): BatchNorm2d(32, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (6): ReLU()\n","    (7): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (8): Conv2d(32, 64, kernel_size=(5, 5), stride=(1, 1), padding=(2, 2))\n","    (9): BatchNorm2d(64, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (10): ReLU()\n","  )\n","  (column3): Sequential(\n","    (0): Conv2d(3, 20, kernel_size=(7, 7), stride=(1, 1), padding=(3, 3))\n","    (1): BatchNorm2d(20, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (2): ReLU()\n","    (3): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (4): Conv2d(20, 40, kernel_size=(5, 5), stride=(1, 1), padding=(2, 2))\n","    (5): BatchNorm2d(40, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (6): ReLU()\n","    (7): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (8): Conv2d(40, 80, kernel_size=(3, 3), stride=(1, 1), padding=(1, 1))\n","    (9): BatchNorm2d(80, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (10): ReLU()\n","  )\n","  (column4): Sequential(\n","    (0): Conv2d(3, 24, kernel_size=(5, 5), stride=(1, 1), padding=(2, 2))\n","    (1): BatchNorm2d(24, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (2): ReLU()\n","    (3): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (4): Conv2d(24, 48, kernel_size=(3, 3), stride=(1, 1), padding=(1, 1))\n","    (5): BatchNorm2d(48, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (6): ReLU()\n","    (7): MaxPool2d(kernel_size=2, stride=2, padding=0, dilation=1, ceil_mode=False)\n","    (8): Conv2d(48, 96, kernel_size=(3, 3), stride=(1, 1), padding=(1, 1))\n","    (9): BatchNorm2d(96, eps=1e-05, momentum=0.1, affine=True, track_running_stats=True)\n","    (10): ReLU()\n","  )\n","  (fusion): Sequential(\n","    (0): Conv2d(304, 64, kernel_size=(1, 1), stride=(1, 1))\n","    (1): ReLU()\n","    (2): Conv2d(64, 1, kernel_size=(1, 1), stride=(1, 1))\n","    (3): ReLU()\n","  )\n",")"]},"execution_count":12,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["model"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"id":"36285b0c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.380948Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.380714Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.386537Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.386052Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.016514,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.387816+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.371302+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["import torch\n","import torch.nn as nn\n","\n","# Defines a custom loss function class\n","class CombinedLoss(nn.Module):            \n","    # Initializes the loss weights\n","    def __init__(self, weight_dmap=0.9, weight_sum_gt=0.1):  \n","        # Initializes the parent nn.Module class\n","        super(CombinedLoss, self).__init__()                 \n","\n","        # Gives 90% importance to density-map loss\n","        self.weight_dmap = weight_dmap      \n","        # Gives 10% importance to total-count loss\n","        self.weight_sum_gt = weight_sum_gt  \n","\n","        # Creates MSE loss for pixel-wise density-map comparison\n","        self.img_loss = nn.MSELoss()        \n","        # Creates MAE/L1 loss for total-count comparison\n","        self.gt_loss_mae = nn.L1Loss()      \n","\n","    # Defines how the combined loss is calculated\n","    def forward(self, predications, density_maps, gt_counts):\n","        # Converts ground-truth counts to floating-point values\n","        gt_counts = gt_counts.float()                       \n","        \n","        # Calculates pixel-wise MSE between predicted and GT density maps\n","        img_loss = self.img_loss(predications, density_maps)        \n","\n","        # Sums all pixels to obtain predicted object counts\n","        pred_counts = torch.squeeze(predications.sum(dim=(2,3)))\n","\n","        # Calculates MAE between predicted and true counts\n","        gt_loss_mae = self.gt_loss_mae(pred_counts, gt_counts)  \n","\n","        # Combines both losses using their weights\n","        combined_loss = self.weight_dmap * img_loss + self.weight_sum_gt * gt_loss_mae  \n","\n","        return combined_loss, gt_loss_mae"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"723c7723","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00877,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.405474+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.396704+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# CombinedLoss class\n","\n","This creates a **custom loss function**. Instead of using only one objective, i train the model using **two objectives**:\n","\n","1. Make the predicted density map look like the ground truth density map.\n","2. Make the total predicted count close to the actual number of people.\n","\n","This implementation uses:\n","\n","```python\n","weight_dmap=0.9\n","weight_sum_gt=0.1\n","```\n","\n","So:\n","\n","$$\n","L = 0.9L_{density} + 0.1L_{count}\n","$$\n","\n","The density map objective gets 90% importance, while the count objective gets 10%. \n","\n","## Why two losses?\n","\n","This is very important.\n","\n","Suppose the actual density map is:\n","\n","```text\n","GT:\n","\n","0 0 1 0 0\n","0 2 3 2 0\n","0 1 2 1 0\n","```\n","\n","The model could produce:\n","\n","```text\n","Prediction:\n","\n","0 1 1 1 0\n","1 1 2 1 1\n","0 1 1 1 0\n","```\n","\n","The spatial distribution may be wrong even if the total count is approximately correct.\n","\n","Conversely, the model could produce a density map with excellent spatial similarity but a slightly incorrect total.\n","\n","Therefore, you have two requirements:\n","\n","1. **Requirement 1:** Predict **where** people are.\n","2. **Requirement 2:** Predict **how many** people there are.\n","\n","The two losses address those two requirements.\n","\n","## MSE density map loss\n","\n","I define:\n","\n","```python\n","self.img_loss = nn.MSELoss()\n","```\n","\n","MSE means: **Mean Squared Error**\n","\n","Mathematically:\n","\n","$$\n","L_{MSE}\n","=\n","\\frac{1}{N}\n","\\sum_i\n","(\\hat{D}_i-D_i)^2\n","$$\n","\n","where:\n","\n","* $D_i$ = ground truth density\n","* $\\hat D_i$ = predicted density\n","\n","So every density map pixel contributes to the loss.\n","\n","If the model predicts:\n","\n","```text\n","GT = 2\n","Prediction = 2\n","```\n","\n","error:\n","\n","$$\n","(2-2)^2=0\n","$$\n","\n","But if:\n","\n","```text\n","GT = 2\n","Prediction = 5\n","```\n","\n","then:\n","\n","$$\n","(5-2)^2=9\n","$$\n","\n","So large density errors are penalized more strongly.\n","\n","## Count loss\n","\n","I define:\n","\n","```python\n","self.gt_loss_mae = nn.L1Loss()\n","```\n","\n","L1 loss is equivalent to **Mean Absolute Error**.\n","\n","$$\n","MAE =\n","\\frac{1}{N}\n","\\sum_i |\\hat C_i-C_i|\n","$$\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","Actual = 100\n","Predicted = 108\n","```\n","\n","then:\n","\n","$$\n","|108-100|=8\n","$$\n","\n","So count error is 8 people.\n","\n","## Forward pass of the loss\n","\n","My function is:\n","\n","```python\n","def forward(self, predications, batch_dmap, batch_gts):\n","```\n","\n","There are three inputs.\n","\n","1. `predications`\n","\n","This is actually the predicted density map from the model.\n","\n","Despite the name `predications`, it isn't a conventional classification prediction tensor here.\n","\n","It is:\n","\n","```text\n","Predicted density map\n","```\n","2. `density_maps`: Ground truth density maps.\n","3. `gt_counts`: Ground truth person counts.\n","\n","![Combined Loss](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/spl_03/main/images/combinedloss.png)\n","\n","### Converting ground-truth counts\n","\n","```python\n","batch_gts = batch_gts.float()\n","```\n","\n","The model works with floating point tensors.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","| Before | After |\n","| --- | --- |\n","| `8` | `8.0` |\n","| `15` | `15.0` |\n","| `23` | `23.0` |\n","\n","### Density map loss\n","\n","```python\n","img_loss = self.img_loss(predications, density_maps)\n","```\n","\n","This compares:\n","\n","```text\n","Predicted density map\n","        VS\n","Ground-truth density map\n","```\n","\n","using MSE.\n","\n","### Obtaining predicted count\n","\n","This is one of the most important lines:\n","\n","```python\n","pred_counts = torch.squeeze(predications.sum(dim=(2,3)))\n","```\n","- `torch.squeeze()` removes dimensions of size 1 from a tensor.\n","\n","```python\n","x = torch.tensor([[[8, 15, 23]]])\n","\n","print(x.shape)\n","# torch.Size([1, 1, 3])\n","\n","y = torch.squeeze(x)\n","\n","print(y)\n","# tensor([ 8, 15, 23])\n","\n","print(y.shape)\n","# torch.Size([3])\n","\n","```\n","Let's understand the tensor dimensions.\n","\n","Suppose the output is:\n","\n","```text\n","[B, 1, H, W]\n","```\n","\n","where:\n","\n","* B = batch size\n","* 1 = density-map channel\n","* H = height\n","* W = width\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","[8, 1, 192, 192]\n","```\n","\n","Then:\n","\n","```python\n","predications.sum(dim=(2,3))\n","```\n","\n","means:\n","\n","> Sum across height and width.\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","density map\n","     ↓\n","sum every pixel\n","     ↓\n","one number\n","```\n","\n","For one image:\n","\n","```text\n","density map\n","       ↓\n","     SUM\n","       ↓\n","  125.7\n","```\n","\n","The predicted crowd count is therefore:\n","\n","$$\n","\\hat C = \\sum_{x,y}\\hat D(x,y)\n","$$\n","\n","### Count MAE\n","\n","Then:\n","\n","```python\n","gt_loss_mae = self.gt_loss_mae(pred_counts, gt_counts)\n","```\n","\n","The predicted counts are compared against the true counts.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","Actual counts:\n","[100, 80, 120]\n","\n","Predicted:\n","[103, 76, 117]\n","```\n","\n","Absolute errors:\n","\n","```text\n","3\n","4\n","3\n","```\n","\n","Mean:\n","\n","$$\n","MAE=\\frac{3+4+3}{3}=3.33\n","$$\n","\n","### Combined loss\n","\n","Finally:\n","\n","```python\n","combined_loss = (self.weight_dmap * img_loss + self.weight_sum_gt * gt_loss_mae)\n","```\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","$$\n","L =\n","0.9L_{MSE}\n","+\n","0.1L_{MAE}\n","$$\n","\n","This is what the optimizer ultimately tries to minimize."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"id":"22059d76","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.423848Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.423639Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.428499Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.427715Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.015914,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.429807+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.413893+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["import torch.optim as optim\n","\n","criterion = CombinedLoss(weight_dmap=0.9, weight_sum_gt=0.1)\n","optimizer = optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=1e-4)\n","scheduler = optim.lr_scheduler.StepLR(optimizer, step_size=10, gamma=0.1)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2b016223","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.008893,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.447388+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.438495+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["* `criterion(...)` calls `forward()` because criterion is an `nn.Module`, It has special behaviour.\n","\n","# Optimizer\n","\n","Adam is the optimization algorithm.\n","\n","Its job is to update model parameters.\n","\n","Conceptually:\n","\n","```text\n","Current weights\n","      ↓\n","Calculate loss\n","      ↓\n","Calculate gradients\n","      ↓\n","    Adam\n","      ↓\n","Updated weights\n","```\n","\n","## Adam vs Other Optimizers\n","\n","A useful way to understand Adam is to compare it with the major alternatives.\n","\n","| Optimizer | Main Idea | Strength |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| **SGD** | Follow the current gradient | Simple, often excellent with good tuning |\n","| **Momentum SGD** | Gradient + accumulated direction | Smoother and faster movement |\n","| **AdaGrad** | Adapt learning rate using past squared gradients | Good for sparse features |\n","| **RMSProp** | Adapt learning rate using recent squared gradients | Handles changing gradient scales |\n","| **Adam** | Momentum + adaptive learning rates | Good general-purpose default |\n","\n","> **Adam essentially combines the important ideas of Momentum + RMSProp.**\n","\n","\n","# Learning rate\n","\n","The learning rate controls how large each update is.\n","\n","Too large:\n","\n","```text\n","training may become unstable\n","```\n","\n","Too small:\n","\n","```text\n","training may be extremely slow\n","```\n","\n","# Learning rate scheduler\n","\n","This means every 10 epochs:\n","\n","$$\n","LR_{new}=0.1\\times LR_{old}\n","$$\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","Epoch 1–10:\n","1e-4\n","\n","Epoch 11–20:\n","1e-5\n","\n","Epoch 21–30:\n","1e-6\n","\n","Epoch 31–40:\n","1e-7\n","```\n","\n","and so on.\n","\n","The actual code calls:\n","\n","```python\n","scheduler.step()\n","```\n","\n","after each epoch. "]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":15,"id":"e0203fe5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.465483Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.465145Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.47058Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.469766Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.016104,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.471869+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.455765+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","Output directory: /kaggle/working/mcnn_results\n"]}],"source":["NUM_EPOCHS = 100\n","\n","PATIENCE = 30\n","OUTPUT_DIR = Path(\"/kaggle/working/mcnn_results\")\n","\n","OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","BEST_MODEL_PATH = (OUTPUT_DIR / \"mcnn_best.pth\")\n","LATEST_MODEL_PATH = (OUTPUT_DIR / \"mcnn_latest.pth\")\n","HISTORY_CSV_PATH = (OUTPUT_DIR / \"mcnn_training_history.csv\")\n","\n","print(\"\\nOutput directory:\", OUTPUT_DIR)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a1e702d4","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.008873,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.489823+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.48095+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Training configuration\n","\n","The code specifies:\n","\n","```python\n","NUM_EPOCHS = 100\n","```\n","\n","Maximum:\n","\n","```text\n","100 epochs\n","```\n","\n","But it doesn't necessarily run all 100.\n","\n","Because:\n","\n","```python\n","PATIENCE = 30\n","```\n","\n","is used for early stopping.\n","\n","> Patience is the number of epochs you wait for the validation performance to improve before stopping training.\n","\n","## Epoch\n","\n","One epoch means:\n","\n","> The model has processed the entire training dataset once.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","360 training images\n","batch size = 8\n","```\n","\n","approximately:\n","\n","$$\n","360/8=45\n","$$\n","\n","batches per epoch.\n","\n","## Best model\n","\n","`mcnn_best.pth` stores the model state corresponding to the best validation loss.\n","\n","This is important because the last epoch isn't necessarily the best epoch.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","Epoch 10 → val loss = 0.50\n","Epoch 20 → val loss = 0.35\n","Epoch 30 → val loss = 0.28\n","Epoch 40 → val loss = 0.31\n","```\n","\n","Best:\n","\n","```text\n","Epoch 30\n","```\n","\n","So you want epoch 30's model, not epoch 40's.\n","\n","## Latest checkpoint\n","\n","`mcnn_latest.pth` stores the most recent model state.\n","\n","This is useful if training gets interrupted.\n","\n","You can potentially resume from the latest checkpoint.\n","\n","## Training history\n","\n","The CSV contains:\n","\n","```text\n","epoch\n","train_loss\n","val_loss\n","train_mae\n","val_mae\n","is_best_epoch\n","```\n","\n","This allows you to plot:\n","\n","```text\n","Loss vs Epoch\n","MAE vs Epoch\n","```\n","\n","and identify:\n","\n","* convergence\n","* overfitting\n","* underfitting\n","* best epoch"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":16,"id":"4743f084","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.508828Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.508464Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.512663Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.511819Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.015313,"end_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.514246+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-21T15:10:14.498933+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["train_losses = []\n","val_losses = []\n","\n","train_mae_